Finding: {"title":"Publish and publish-selected event-insert loops are not batched — N sequential awaited inserts inside one transaction","severity":"LOW","area":"Performance / N+1","files":["src/server/routes/routes-ai-schedule.ts"],"detail":"Both /drafts/:draftId/publish (lines 812-834) and /publish-selected (lines 1290-1312) insert schedule_events one row at a time in a for-loop with `await tx.insert(...).returning()` per event, rather than a single batched `.values([...])` insert.","impact":"For a large weekly draft (potentially dozens to 100+ events), this serializes N round-trips to Postgres inside one transaction, increasing transaction hold time and publish latency proportionally to event count.","recommendation":"Switch to a single batched insert (`tx.insert(schema.scheduleEvents).values(toPublish.map(...)).returning()`) — Drizzle supports multi-row insert natively; this also shrinks the transaction's lock window.","confidence":"medium"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

